  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p><strong>Today is the last day to register for my upcoming webinar: Why Do Vegetarians Have Higher Stroke Risk?</strong></p><strong>\n</strong><p><strong>Date and Time:</strong> February 19, 2-4pm ET<br/>\n<strong>Last Day to Register:</strong> February 13, TODAY</p>\n<p>Given that high blood pressure and inadequate fruit and vegetable consumption are among the most important stroke risk factors, you would assume those eating plant-based diets would be at significantly lower risk, just as they are with heart attacks. You might be surprised to learn that there had never been any studies on the incidence of stroke in vegetarians, though…until now. And if you think that is surprising, wait until you hear the results. Yes, they had lower heart disease risk as expected, but those eating meat-free diets appeared to have more stroke risk. If that is indeed the case, what might be the cause, and what can we do about it?</p>\n<p>To see the list of topics I’ll cover, go <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/webinar/vegetarians-higher-stroke-risk/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a>.</p>\n<p>UPDATE: Get the download of this webinar <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads/products/vegetarian-stroke-risk-digital\">here</a>, and to be the first to see announcements of future webinars, be sure you <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\">subscribe</a> to our newsletter.</p>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Past Webinars Available</h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/Webinar-Downloads-Stacked.png/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-62510 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/Webinar-Downloads-Stacked.png\" alt=\"Webinar-Downloads\" width=\"200\" height=\"371\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/Webinar-Downloads-Stacked.png 731w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/Webinar-Downloads-Stacked-720x1334.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/Webinar-Downloads-Stacked-540x1000.png 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>The videos from my most recent webinar, What Triggered the Obesity Epidemic?, are now available for digital download <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads/products/obesity-epidemic-digital\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads/products/obesity-epidemic-digital\">here</a>. </p>\n<p>In fact, all of my previous webinars are available:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads/products/fasting-weight-loss-digital\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads/products/fasting-weight-loss-digital\">Intermittent Fasting</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads/products/fasting-disease-reversal-digital\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads/products/fasting-disease-reversal-digital\">Fasting for Disease Reversal</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads/products/fasting-cancer-digital\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads/products/fasting-cancer-digital\">Fasting and Cancer</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads/products/cannabis-what-does-the-science-say-digital\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads/products/cannabis-what-does-the-science-say-digital\">Cannabis</a></li>\n</ul>\n<div>Many of the videos from those webinars are already up on NutritionFacts.org, but if you’d like them all in one place, check out the downloads. Note that these are just the videos from the webinars, and do not include the live Q&amp;As.</div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>\n<h4>Seeking Spanish Volunteers</h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/VolunteerGraphic_IG-Spanish.png/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-large wp-image-58779 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/VolunteerGraphic_IG-Spanish-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"Spanish volunteers needed\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/VolunteerGraphic_IG-Spanish-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/VolunteerGraphic_IG-Spanish-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/VolunteerGraphic_IG-Spanish-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/VolunteerGraphic_IG-Spanish-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/VolunteerGraphic_IG-Spanish-1200x1200.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/VolunteerGraphic_IG-Spanish-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/VolunteerGraphic_IG-Spanish-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/04/VolunteerGraphic_IG-Spanish.png 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Our Spanish team is looking for a few experienced translators to work on translating and editing transcripts, blog posts, and video subtitles. Applicants should be proficient in both Spanish and English, with previous translation experience and a basic understanding of NutritionFacts.org content and medical terms. Go <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/volunteer/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a> to apply.  </p></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>\n<h4 class=\"null\">New B12 Recommendations</h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/B12-Bottle-on-Blue-e1581352421528.jpeg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-large wp-image-62506 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/B12-Bottle-on-Blue-e1581352421528-1024x1024.jpeg\" alt=\"B12 update\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/B12-Bottle-on-Blue-e1581352421528-1024x1024.jpeg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/B12-Bottle-on-Blue-e1581352421528-960x960.jpeg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/B12-Bottle-on-Blue-e1581352421528-768x768.jpeg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/B12-Bottle-on-Blue-e1581352421528-500x500.jpeg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/B12-Bottle-on-Blue-e1581352421528-1200x1200.jpeg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/B12-Bottle-on-Blue-e1581352421528-720x720.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/B12-Bottle-on-Blue-e1581352421528-540x540.jpeg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>I want to make sure everyone knows that my B12 supplement recommendations have changed based on new research. The most up-to-date info can always be found on my <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/optimum-nutrient-recommendations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Optimum Nutrition Recommendations</a> page, but here they are for easy reference: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>At least 2,000 mcg (µg) cyanocobalamin once each week, ideally as a chewable, sublingual, or liquid supplement taken on an empty stomach\n<ul>\n<li><em>or</em> at least 50 mcg daily of supplemental cyanocobalamin (you needn’t worry about taking too much)</li>\n<li><em>or</em> servings of B12-fortified foods three times a day (at each meal), each containing at least 190% of the Daily Value listed on the nutrition facts label (based on the new labeling mandated to start January 1, 2020—the target is 4.5 mcg three times a day). </li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Those over 65 years of age should take at least 1,000 mcg (µg) cyanocobalamin every day.</li>\n<li>Tip: If experiencing deficiency symptoms, the best test is probably urine MMA (<em>not</em> serum B12 level)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I’ve got a series of new videos coming out explaining the changes that will be featured in an upcoming webinar—stay tuned!</p></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>\n<h4>Dr. Barnard’s New Book</h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/serveimage.jpeg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-62512 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/serveimage.jpeg\" alt=\"Dr. Barnards new book\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\"/></a>My dear friend and colleague, Dr. Neal Barnard, just released his new book. <a href=\"https://www.pcrm.org/yourbodyinbalance\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.pcrm.org/yourbodyinbalance\">Your Body in Balance</a> on how foods affect our hormones and the simple dietary changes that can help. This book provides step-by-step guidance on how specific foods can help with infertility, cramps, endometriosis, PCOS, hot flashes, and erectile dysfunction, as well as breast and prostate cancer through evidence-based dietary change. It also discusses how foods affect our weight, mood, and overall health. Learn more <a href=\"https://www.pcrm.org/yourbodyinbalance\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.pcrm.org/yourbodyinbalance\">here</a>.</p></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-large wp-image-60211\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png\" alt=\"Top 3 Videos of the Month\" width=\"460\" height=\"149\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-960x310.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-768x248.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-720x233.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-540x174.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png 1108w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 460px) 100vw, 460px\"/></a></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-08.jpeg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-61507 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-08.jpeg\" alt=\"Breakfast Like a King, Lunch Like a Prince, Dinner Like a Pauper\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-08.jpeg 1920w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-08-960x540.jpeg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-08-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-08-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-08-480x270.jpeg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-08-1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-08-720x405.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-08-540x304.jpeg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/breakfast-like-a-king-lunch-like-a-prince-dinner-like-a-pauper/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Breakfast Like a King, Lunch Like a Prince, Dinner Like a Pauper</a><p></p>\n<p>Harness the power of your circadian rhythms for weight loss by making breakfast or lunch your main meal of the day.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-06.jpeg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-61491 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-06.jpeg\" alt=\"Eat More Calories in the Morning to Lose Weight\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-06.jpeg 1920w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-06-960x540.jpeg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-06-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-06-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-06-480x270.jpeg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-06-1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-06-720x405.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/01/49-06-540x304.jpeg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/eat-more-calories-in-the-morning-to-lose-weight/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Eat More Calories in the Morning to Lose Weight</a></p>\n<p>\nA calorie is not a calorie—it not only depends on what you eat, but when you eat.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/49-10.jpeg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-61697 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/49-10-960x540.jpeg\" alt=\"Benefits of Grapes for Brain Health\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/49-10-960x540.jpeg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/49-10-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/49-10-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/49-10-480x270.jpeg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/49-10-1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/49-10-720x405.jpeg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/49-10-540x304.jpeg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/02/49-10.jpeg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/benefits-of-grapes-for-brain-health/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Benefits of Grapes for Brain Health</a></p>\n<p>Grape juice and whole grapes are put to the test for brain function, including cognitive decline in early Alzheimer’s.</p>\n</div>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Live Q&amp;As February 20</h4>\n<div><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square.png/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-large wp-image-53879 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"Live Q&amp;A\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1200x1200.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square.png 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Every month now I do Q&amp;As live from my treadmill, and <em><strong>Feb 20</strong></em> is the day.</div>\n<div> </div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Facebook Live</strong>: At 12:00 p.m. ET go to our <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\">Facebook page</a> to watch live and ask questions.</li>\n<li><strong>YouTube Live Stream: </strong>At 1:00 p.m. ET go <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\">here</a> to watch live and ask even more questions! </li>\n</ul>\n<div>You can now find links to all of my past live YouTube and Facebook Q&amp;As right <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a> on NutritionFacts.org. If that’s not enough, remember I have an audio podcast to keep you company at <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/audio/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://nutritionfacts.org/audio.</a></div>\n<div> </div>\n<p>Thanks to the launch of <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">How Not to Diet</a>, I’ve been doing tons of interviews in between my <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/pages/speaking-dates\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://drgreger.org/pages/speaking-dates\">speaking engagements</a> (including <a href=\"https://www.lotushealthfoundation.org/community-of-wellness-2020\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.lotushealthfoundation.org/community-of-wellness-2020\">Rochester, MN</a>, <a href=\"http://www.savannahvegfest.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"http://www.savannahvegfest.org\">Savannah</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/spring-into-health-speaker-series-dr-michael-greger-tickets-86123781549\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/spring-into-health-speaker-series-dr-michael-greger-tickets-86123781549\">Lakeland, FL</a>, to name just a few). Check out this recent one on <a href=\"https://www.humnutrition.com/blog/how-not-to-diet-by-dr-michael-greger/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.humnutrition.com/blog/how-not-to-diet-by-dr-michael-greger/\">The Wellnest blog</a> for an overview of what’s in the new book! </p>\n<div> </div>\n<div>In health,<br/>\n<b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b><p></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><b>here</b></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2019: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\"><b>Evidence-Based Weight Loss</b></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><u><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><u><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><u><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><u><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><u><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></u></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>"
